<div id="rubymem">
  <%= render :partial => "shared/header" %>

  <section>

    <div class="new-vuln">
      <h3>Advisory form</h3>
      <%= render :partial => "form", :locals => { :presenter => @presenter, :preview_label => "Preview" } %>
    </div>

    <div class="new-vuln">
      <h2>Report a new leak</h2>
      <p>Hey! Thanks for taking the time to do this. Your submission helps the community. All submissions to this website are ultimately vetted on the <a href="https://github.com/rubymem/ruby-mem-advisory-db">GitHub repository</a>.</p>
      <h4>Reporting a leak takes three steps.</h4>
      <ol>
        <li>Fill out the form to the left.</li>
        <li>Review the preview. We turn your report into the YAML that goes into the
          advisory database, so you can revise anything that looks out of place.</li>
        <li>Submit for review. That is when we store it and email the reviewers,
          nothing is saved before it.</li>
      </ol>
      <h4>Before you start</h4>
      <ul>
        <li>If it is a vulnerability, discreetly disclose the flaw to the gem
          maintainer(s) first. Please be polite! Open source maintainers are usually
          unpaid volunteers, and everyone deserves a little courtesy.</li>
        <li>Try to figure out what versions are affected by the flaw, and whether a
          patch can be released.</li>
      </ul>
      <br/>
    </div>

  </section>
</div>
